  "analysis": "Both responses address the single-writer limitation and propose sharding, but HCJ provides a more thorough design (ADR, test harness, budget dry‑run, explicit failure isolation) and aligns gates with cost windows and rollback constraints. HMT focuses on provisioning extra volumes without detailed cost or risk analysis and omits some of the nuanced constraints (e.g., compute budget caps, detailed rollback handling). HCJ therefore offers a clearer, more actionable plan with fewer likely follow‑up questions.",
